IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa13-ch2-allotment.l4: the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 17 Chapter 2 (ss 549 to 559): allotment of shares,
-- general provisions. Lines 7605-7715 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1: the law, objectively, written from the text alone.
-- How to read an answer: see the header of coa13-ch1-shares.l4 (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE "the text says no in its own words",
-- NOTHING "not covered"). Money is NUMBER in pounds sterling; every name begins with the section label it implements.
--
-- A period "within two months" or "within one month" after the allotment is counted as the library's `add months`
-- counts it (the same day of the month, or the last day of a shorter month): fork F-periods in NOTES.md.

§ `Part 17, Chapter 2: Allotment of shares: general provisions`

§§ `Power of directors to allot shares (ss 549 to 551)`

-- ---- s 549: Exercise by directors of power to allot shares etc -------------------------------------------

-- src:7613 | (a) to the allotment of shares in pursuance of an employees' share scheme, or
-- src:7614 | (b) to the grant of a right to subscribe for, or to convert any security into, shares so allotted.
@ref s 549(2) subsection (1) does not apply to an employees' share scheme (src:7613-7614)
GIVEN `s 1166 the scheme is an employees' share scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the exercise is the allotment of shares in pursuance of the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exercise is the grant of a right to subscribe for, or to convert any security into, shares so allotted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 549(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the exercise` MEANS
    IF `the exercise is the allotment of shares in pursuance of the scheme` OR `the exercise is the grant of a right to subscribe for, or to convert any security into, shares so allotted`
    THEN `s 1166 the scheme is an employees' share scheme` -- JUST TRUE: the exercise is within (a) or (b); NOTHING (points outside the text) passes through; JUST FALSE is s 1166's no
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (1) does not apply (a) to the allotment of shares in pursuance of an employees' share scheme, or (b) to the grant of a right"

-- src:7615 | (3) Subsection (1) does not apply to the allotment of shares pursuant to a right to subscribe for, or to convert any security into, shares in the company.
@ref s 549(3) subsection (1) does not apply to allotment pursuant to a right (src:7615)
GIVEN `the exercise is the allotment of shares pursuant to a right to subscribe for, or to convert any security into, shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 549(3) subsection (1) does not apply to the allotment` MEANS
    IF `the exercise is the allotment of shares pursuant to a right to subscribe for, or to convert any security into, shares in the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (1) does not apply to the allotment of shares pursuant to a right"

-- src:7616 | (3A) Subsection (1) does not apply to anything done for the purposes of a compromise or arrangement sanctioned in accordance with Part 26A (arrangements and reconstructions: companies in financial difficulty).
@ref s 549(3A) subsection (1) does not apply to a compromise or arrangement under Part 26A (src:7616)
GIVEN `it is done for the purposes of a compromise or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Part 26A the compromise or arrangement is sanctioned in accordance with Part 26A` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 549(3A) subsection (1) does not apply to the thing done` MEANS
    IF `it is done for the purposes of a compromise or arrangement`
    THEN `Part 26A the compromise or arrangement is sanctioned in accordance with Part 26A` -- the Part 26A answer is passed through (JUST FALSE is Part 26A's no; NOTHING points outside the text)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not apply to anything done for the purposes of a compromise or arrangement sanctioned in accordance with Part 26A"

-- s 550 and s 551 are written below; s 549(1) takes their answers (and those above) as inputs.

-- src:7608 | (1) The directors of a company must not exercise any power of the company—
-- src:7609 | (a) to allot shares in the company, or
-- src:7610 | (b) to grant rights to subscribe for, or to convert any security into, shares in the company,
-- src:7611 | except in accordance with section 550 (private company with single class of shares) or section 551 (authorisation by company).
@ref s 549(1) directors must not exercise the power except in accordance with s 550 or s 551 (src:7608-7611)
GIVEN `the power is to allot shares in the company or to grant rights to subscribe for, or to convert any security into, shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 550 the directors may exercise the power under section 550` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 551(1) the directors may exercise the power under section 551` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 549(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the exercise` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 549(3) subsection (1) does not apply to the allotment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 549(3A) subsection (1) does not apply to the thing done` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 549(1) the directors are prohibited from exercising the power` MEANS
    IF `the power is to allot shares in the company or to grant rights to subscribe for, or to convert any security into, shares in the company`
    THEN IF     `s 550 the directors may exercise the power under section 550` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             OR `s 551(1) the directors may exercise the power under section 551` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             OR `s 549(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the exercise` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             OR `s 549(3) subsection (1) does not apply to the allotment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             OR `s 549(3A) subsection (1) does not apply to the thing done` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except in accordance with section 550 ... or section 551" and "Subsection (1) does not apply" (an exception met)
         ELSE JUST TRUE -- no exception is shown to apply: the prohibition stands (fork F-549: an exception that answers NOTHING is read as not shown to apply)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any power of the company (a) to allot shares ... or (b) to grant rights"

-- src:7617 | (4) A director who knowingly contravenes, or permits or authorises a contravention of, this section commits an offence.
@ref s 549(4) offence: a director who knowingly contravenes, or permits or authorises a contravention (src:7617)
GIVEN `the director knowingly contravenes, or permits or authorises a contravention of, section 549` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 549(4) the director commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the director knowingly contravenes, or permits or authorises a contravention of, section 549`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A director who knowingly contravenes, or permits or authorises a contravention of, this section commits an offence"

-- src:7618 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:7619 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:7620 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 549(5)(a) penalty on conviction on indictment (src:7618-7620)
`s 549(5)(a) penalty on conviction on indictment` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
    `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
    `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
    `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

@ref s 549(5)(b) penalty on summary conviction (src:7620)
`s 549(5)(b) penalty on summary conviction` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
    `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)
    `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
    `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

@ref s 549(5) a person guilty of an offence under s 549 is liable (src:7618-7620)
GIVETH A LIST OF Penalty
`s 549(5) the penalties for an offence under section 549` MEANS
    LIST `s 549(5)(a) penalty on conviction on indictment`, `s 549(5)(b) penalty on summary conviction`

-- src:7621 | (6) Nothing in this section affects the validity of an allotment or other transaction.
@ref s 549(6) nothing in this section affects the validity of an allotment or other transaction (src:7621)
GIVEN `the matter is an allotment or other transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 549(6) section 549 makes the allotment or other transaction invalid` MEANS
    IF `the matter is an allotment or other transaction`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section affects the validity of an allotment or other transaction"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of an allotment or other transaction only

-- ---- s 550: private company with only one class of shares ------------------------------------------------

-- src:7623 | Where a private company has only one class of shares, the directors may exercise any power of the company—
-- src:7624 | (a) to allot shares of that class, or
-- src:7625 | (b) to grant rights to subscribe for or to convert any security into such shares,
-- src:7626 | except to the extent that they are prohibited from doing so by the company's articles.
@ref s 550 directors of a private company with one class of shares may allot unless the articles prohibit (src:7623-7626)
GIVEN `s 4(1) the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has only one class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power is to allot shares of that class or to grant rights to subscribe for or to convert any security into such shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's articles prohibit the directors from doing so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 550 the directors may exercise the power under section 550` MEANS
    IF     `s 4(1) the company is a private company`
       AND `the company has only one class of shares`
       AND `the power is to allot shares of that class or to grant rights to subscribe for or to convert any security into such shares`
    THEN IF `the company's articles prohibit the directors from doing so`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except to the extent that they are prohibited from doing so by the company's articles"
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a private company has only one class of shares" (a "where" that fails)

-- ---- s 551: authorisation by company ---------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7628 | (1) The directors of a company may exercise a power of the company—
-- src:7629 | (a) to allot shares in the company, or
-- src:7630 | (b) to grant rights to subscribe for or to convert any security into shares in the company,
-- src:7631 | if they are authorised to do so by the company's articles or by resolution of the company.
@ref s 551(1) directors may exercise the power if authorised by the articles or by resolution (src:7628-7631)
GIVEN `the power is to allot shares in the company or to grant rights to subscribe for or to convert any security into shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors are authorised by the company's articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors are authorised by resolution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 551(1) the directors may exercise the power under section 551` MEANS
    IF `the power is to allot shares in the company or to grant rights to subscribe for or to convert any security into shares in the company`
    THEN IF `the directors are authorised by the company's articles` OR `the directors are authorised by resolution of the company`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if they are authorised to do so by the company's articles or by resolution of the company" (a grant: a failed condition is not the text's no, fork F-grant-gate)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a power of the company (a) to allot shares in the company, or (b) to grant rights"

-- src:7632 | (2) Authorisation may be given for a particular exercise of the power or for its exercise generally, and may be unconditional or subject to conditions.
@ref s 551(2) authorisation may be particular or general, unconditional or conditional (src:7632)
GIVEN `it is given for a particular exercise of the power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is given for the exercise of the power generally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is unconditional` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is subject to conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 551(2) the authorisation may be given in this way` MEANS
    IF     (`it is given for a particular exercise of the power` OR `it is given for the exercise of the power generally`)
       AND (`it is unconditional` OR `it is subject to conditions`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Authorisation may be given for a particular exercise of the power or for its exercise generally, and may be unconditional or subject to conditions"

-- src:7634 | (a) state the maximum amount of shares that may be allotted under it, and
@ref s 551(3)(a) authorisation must state the maximum amount of shares (src:7634)
GIVEN `the authorisation states the maximum amount of shares that may be allotted under it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 551(3)(a) the authorisation meets the requirement to state the maximum amount of shares` MEANS
    IF `the authorisation states the maximum amount of shares that may be allotted under it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Authorisation must (a) state the maximum amount of shares that may be allotted under it" (a bare "must" not done: a fork line)

-- src:7635 | (b) specify the date on which it will expire, which must be not more than five years from—
-- src:7636 | (i) in the case of authorisation contained in the company's articles at the time of its original incorporation, the date of that incorporation;
-- src:7637 | (ii) in any other case, the date on which the resolution is passed by virtue of which the authorisation is given.
@ref s 551(3)(b) authorisation must specify an expiry date not more than five years away (src:7635-7637)
GIVEN `the authorisation specifies the date on which it will expire` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorisation is contained in the company's articles at the time of its original incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the company's incorporation` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the resolution is passed by virtue of which the authorisation is given` IS A DATE
      `the date specified as the date of expiry` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 551(3)(b) the authorisation meets the requirement to specify an expiry date within five years` MEANS
    IF `the authorisation specifies the date on which it will expire`
    THEN IF `the date specified as the date of expiry` AT MOST `five years from the starting date`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "which must be not more than five years from" the starting date
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must ... (b) specify the date on which it will expire"
    WHERE
        -- (i) articles at the time of the original incorporation: five years from the date of that incorporation;
        -- (ii) any other case: five years from the date on which the resolution is passed.
        `the starting date` MEANS
            IF `the authorisation is contained in the company's articles at the time of its original incorporation`
            THEN `the date of the company's incorporation`
            ELSE `the date on which the resolution is passed by virtue of which the authorisation is given`
        `five years from the starting date` MEANS `add years` `the starting date` 5

-- src:7633 | (3) Authorisation must—
@ref s 551(3) authorisation must state the maximum and specify an expiry date (src:7633)
GIVEN `the authorisation states the maximum amount of shares that may be allotted under it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorisation specifies the date on which it will expire` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorisation is contained in the company's articles at the time of its original incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the company's incorporation` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the resolution is passed by virtue of which the authorisation is given` IS A DATE
      `the date specified as the date of expiry` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 551(3) the authorisation meets the requirements of subsection (3)` MEANS
    IF     `s 551(3)(a) the authorisation meets the requirement to state the maximum amount of shares` `the authorisation states the maximum amount of shares that may be allotted under it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `s 551(3)(b) the authorisation meets the requirement to specify an expiry date within five years` `the authorisation specifies the date on which it will expire` `the authorisation is contained in the company's articles at the time of its original incorporation` `the date of the company's incorporation` `the date on which the resolution is passed by virtue of which the authorisation is given` `the date specified as the date of expiry` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Authorisation must (a) ... and (b) ..." (a bare "must" not done: a fork line)

-- src:7638 | (4) Authorisation may—
-- src:7639 | (a) be renewed or further renewed by resolution of the company for a further period not exceeding five years, and
@ref s 551(4)(a) authorisation may be renewed by resolution for a further period not exceeding five years (src:7638-7639)
GIVEN `the renewal is by resolution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the renewing resolution is passed` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the renewed authorisation will expire` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 551(4)(a) the authorisation may be renewed or further renewed` MEANS
    IF `the renewal is by resolution of the company`
    THEN IF `the date on which the renewed authorisation will expire` AT MOST (`add years` `the date on which the renewing resolution is passed` 5)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a further period not exceeding five years" (the further period is counted from the renewing resolution: fork F-551(4)(a))
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "be renewed or further renewed by resolution of the company"

-- src:7640 | (b) be revoked or varied at any time by resolution of the company.
@ref s 551(4)(b) authorisation may be revoked or varied at any time by resolution (src:7640)
GIVEN `the revocation or variation is by resolution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 551(4)(b) the authorisation may be revoked or varied` MEANS
    IF `the revocation or variation is by resolution of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "be revoked or varied at any time by resolution of the company"

-- src:7642 | (a) state (or restate) the maximum amount of shares that may be allotted under the authorisation or, as the case may be, the amount remaining to be allotted under it, and
@ref s 551(5)(a) renewing resolution must state the maximum or the amount remaining (src:7642)
GIVEN `the resolution states (or restates) the maximum amount of shares that may be allotted under the authorisation or the amount remaining to be allotted under it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 551(5)(a) the resolution meets the requirement to state the maximum or remaining amount` MEANS
    IF `the resolution states (or restates) the maximum amount of shares that may be allotted under the authorisation or the amount remaining to be allotted under it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A resolution renewing authorisation must (a) state (or restate) the maximum amount" (a bare "must" not done: a fork line)

-- src:7643 | (b) specify the date on which the renewed authorisation will expire.
@ref s 551(5)(b) renewing resolution must specify the new expiry date (src:7643)
GIVEN `the resolution specifies the date on which the renewed authorisation will expire` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 551(5)(b) the resolution meets the requirement to specify the expiry date` MEANS
    IF `the resolution specifies the date on which the renewed authorisation will expire`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must ... (b) specify the date on which the renewed authorisation will expire" (a bare "must" not done: a fork line)

-- src:7641 | (5) A resolution renewing authorisation must—
@ref s 551(5) a resolution renewing authorisation must state the amount and specify the date (src:7641)
GIVEN `the resolution states (or restates) the maximum amount of shares that may be allotted under the authorisation or the amount remaining to be allotted under it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution specifies the date on which the renewed authorisation will expire` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 551(5) the resolution renewing the authorisation meets the requirements of subsection (5)` MEANS
    IF     `s 551(5)(a) the resolution meets the requirement to state the maximum or remaining amount` `the resolution states (or restates) the maximum amount of shares that may be allotted under the authorisation or the amount remaining to be allotted under it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `s 551(5)(b) the resolution meets the requirement to specify the expiry date` `the resolution specifies the date on which the renewed authorisation will expire` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A resolution renewing authorisation must (a) ... and (b) ..." (a bare "must" not done: a fork line)

-- src:7644 | (6) In relation to rights to subscribe for or to convert any security into shares in the company, references in this section to the maximum amount of shares that may be allotted under the authorisation are to the maximum amount of shares that may be allotted pursuant to the rights.
@ref s 551(6) references to the maximum amount of shares, in relation to rights to subscribe or convert (src:7644)
GIVEN `the authorisation relates to rights to subscribe for or to convert any security into shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maximum number of shares that may be allotted under the authorisation` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum number of shares that may be allotted pursuant to the rights` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 551(6) the maximum amount of shares that may be allotted under the authorisation, for the purposes of section 551` MEANS
    IF `the authorisation relates to rights to subscribe for or to convert any security into shares in the company`
    THEN `the maximum number of shares that may be allotted pursuant to the rights`
    ELSE `the maximum number of shares that may be allotted under the authorisation`

-- src:7645 | (7) The directors may allot shares, or grant rights to subscribe for or to convert any security into shares, after authorisation has expired if—
-- src:7646 | (a) the shares are allotted, or the rights are granted, in pursuance of an offer or agreement made by the company before the authorisation expired, and
-- src:7647 | (b) the authorisation allowed the company to make an offer or agreement which would or might require shares to be allotted, or rights to be granted, after the authorisation had expired.
@ref s 551(7) directors may allot after the authorisation has expired (src:7645-7647)
GIVEN `the shares are allotted, or the rights are granted, in pursuance of an offer or agreement made by the company before the authorisation expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorisation allowed the company to make an offer or agreement which would or might require shares to be allotted, or rights to be granted, after the authorisation had expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 551(7) the directors may allot shares or grant rights after the authorisation has expired` MEANS
    IF     `the shares are allotted, or the rights are granted, in pursuance of an offer or agreement made by the company before the authorisation expired`
       AND `the authorisation allowed the company to make an offer or agreement which would or might require shares to be allotted, or rights to be granted, after the authorisation had expired`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "after authorisation has expired if (a) ... and (b) ..." (a grant: a failed condition is not the text's no, fork F-grant-gate)

-- src:7648 | (8) A resolution of a company to give, vary, revoke or renew authorisation under this section may be an ordinary resolution, even though it amends the company's articles.
@ref s 551(8) a resolution to give, vary, revoke or renew authorisation may be an ordinary resolution (src:7648)
GIVEN `the resolution is to give, vary, revoke or renew authorisation under section 551` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of resolution` IS A `Kind of resolution`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 551(8) the resolution may be an ordinary resolution` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is to give, vary, revoke or renew authorisation under section 551`
    THEN CONSIDER `the kind of resolution`
         WHEN `an ordinary resolution` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a special resolution` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether a special resolution will serve is s 282(5), not this subsection
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A resolution of a company to give, vary, revoke or renew authorisation under this section"

-- src:7649 | (9) Chapter 3 of Part 3 (resolutions affecting a company's constitution) applies to a resolution under this section.
@ref s 551(9) Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies to a resolution under this section (src:7649)
GIVEN `the resolution is a resolution under section 551` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 551(9) Chapter 3 of Part 3 applies to the resolution` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is a resolution under section 551`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "applies to a resolution under this section"

§§ `Prohibition of commissions, discounts and allowances (ss 552 and 553)`

-- ---- s 553: Permitted commission (written before s 552, which takes its answer) --------------------------

-- src:7660 | (a) the payment of the commission is authorised by the company's articles; and
@ref s 553(2)(a) the payment of the commission must be authorised by the articles (src:7660)
GIVEN `the payment of the commission is authorised by the company's articles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 553(2)(a) the condition that the articles authorise the commission is satisfied` MEANS
    IF `the payment of the commission is authorised by the company's articles`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The conditions are that (a) the payment of the commission is authorised by the company's articles" (a condition of a permission that is not met)

-- src:7661 | (b) the commission paid or agreed to be paid does not exceed—
-- src:7662 | (i) 10% of the price at which the shares are issued, or
-- src:7663 | (ii) the amount or rate authorised by the articles,
-- src:7664 | whichever is the less.
@ref s 553(2)(b) the commission must not exceed the lesser of 10% of the issue price and the amount or rate the articles authorise (src:7661-7664)
GIVEN `the commission paid or agreed to be paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the price at which the shares are issued` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount authorised by the articles (worked out from the rate, if they state a rate)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 553(2)(b) the condition that the commission does not exceed the limit is satisfied` MEANS
    IF `the commission paid or agreed to be paid` AT MOST `the limit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not exceed (i) 10% of the price at which the shares are issued, or (ii) the amount or rate authorised by the articles, whichever is the less"
    WHERE
        `ten per cent of the price at which the shares are issued` MEANS `the price at which the shares are issued` TIMES 0.1
        `the limit` MEANS min `ten per cent of the price at which the shares are issued` `the amount authorised by the articles (worked out from the rate, if they state a rate)`

-- src:7658 | (1) A company may, if the following conditions are satisfied, pay a commission to a person in consideration of his subscribing or agreeing to subscribe (whether absolutely or conditionally) for shares in the company, or procuring or agreeing to procure subscriptions (whether absolute or conditional) for shares in the company.
@ref s 553(1) a company may pay a commission if the conditions are satisfied (src:7658)
GIVEN `the commission is in consideration of the person subscribing or agreeing to subscribe for shares in the company, or procuring or agreeing to procure subscriptions for them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 553(2)(a) the condition that the articles authorise the commission is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 553(2)(b) the condition that the commission does not exceed the limit is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 553(1) the company may pay the commission` MEANS
    IF `the commission is in consideration of the person subscribing or agreeing to subscribe for shares in the company, or procuring or agreeing to procure subscriptions for them`
    THEN IF     `s 553(2)(a) the condition that the articles authorise the commission is satisfied` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            AND `s 553(2)(b) the condition that the commission does not exceed the limit is satisfied` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF     `s 553(2)(a) the condition that the articles authorise the commission is satisfied` EQUALS JUST FALSE
                  OR `s 553(2)(b) the condition that the commission does not exceed the limit is satisfied` EQUALS JUST FALSE
              THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company may, if the following conditions are satisfied, pay a commission" (a grant: a failed condition is not the text's no, fork F-grant-gate)
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a condition's answer is not known
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "pay a commission to a person in consideration of his subscribing ... or procuring"

-- src:7665 | (3) A vendor to, or promoter of, or other person who receives payment in money or shares from, a company may apply any part of the money or shares so received in payment of any commission the payment of which directly by the company would be permitted by this section.
@ref s 553(3) a vendor, promoter or other recipient may apply money or shares in payment of a permitted commission (src:7665)
GIVEN `the person is a vendor to, or promoter of, or other person who receives payment in money or shares from, the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 553(1) the company may pay the commission` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 553(3) the person may apply the money or shares in payment of the commission` MEANS
    IF `the person is a vendor to, or promoter of, or other person who receives payment in money or shares from, the company`
    THEN IF `s 553(1) the company may pay the commission` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any commission the payment of which directly by the company would be permitted by this section"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A vendor to, or promoter of, or other person who receives payment in money or shares from, a company may apply"

-- ---- s 552: General prohibition of commissions, discounts and allowances ---------------------------------

-- src:7652 | (1) Except as permitted by section 553 (permitted commission), a company must not apply any of its shares or capital money, either directly or indirectly, in payment of any commission, discount or allowance to any person in consideration of his—
-- src:7653 | (a) subscribing or agreeing to subscribe (whether absolutely or conditionally) for shares in the company, or
-- src:7654 | (b) procuring or agreeing to procure subscriptions (whether absolute or conditional) for shares in the company.
@ref s 552(1) a company must not apply its shares or capital money in payment of a commission, discount or allowance (src:7652-7654)
GIVEN `the company applies any of its shares or capital money, directly or indirectly, in payment of a commission, discount or allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in consideration of the person subscribing or agreeing to subscribe (whether absolutely or conditionally) for shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in consideration of the person procuring or agreeing to procure subscriptions (whether absolute or conditional) for shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 553(1) the company may pay the commission` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 552(1) the company is prohibited from applying its shares or capital money in payment` MEANS
    IF     `the company applies any of its shares or capital money, directly or indirectly, in payment of a commission, discount or allowance`
       AND (    `it is in consideration of the person subscribing or agreeing to subscribe (whether absolutely or conditionally) for shares in the company`
             OR `it is in consideration of the person procuring or agreeing to procure subscriptions (whether absolute or conditional) for shares in the company`)
    THEN CONSIDER `s 553(1) the company may pay the commission`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except as permitted by section 553 (permitted commission)" (the exception is met)
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE -- no exception is shown to apply: the prohibition stands (fork F-exception: s 553(1) answers NOTHING for a commission outside its conditions, fork F-grant-gate)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in payment of any commission, discount or allowance to any person in consideration of his (a) subscribing ... or (b) procuring"

DECLARE `s 552(2) manner of application` IS ONE OF
    `s 552(2) by being added to the purchase money of property acquired by the company`
    `s 552(2) by being added to the contract price of work to be executed for the company`
    `s 552(2) by being paid out of the nominal purchase money or contract price`
    `s 552(2) in some other way`

-- src:7655 | (2) It is immaterial how the shares or money are so applied, whether by being added to the purchase money of property acquired by the company or to the contract price of work to be executed for the company, or being paid out of the nominal purchase money or contract price, or otherwise.
@ref s 552(2) it is immaterial how the shares or money are applied (src:7655)
GIVEN `the manner of application` IS A `s 552(2) manner of application`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 552(2) the manner of application affects whether the prohibition applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the manner of application`
    WHEN `s 552(2) by being added to the purchase money of property acquired by the company` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is immaterial how the shares or money are so applied"
    WHEN `s 552(2) by being added to the contract price of work to be executed for the company` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is immaterial how the shares or money are so applied"
    WHEN `s 552(2) by being paid out of the nominal purchase money or contract price` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is immaterial how the shares or money are so applied"
    WHEN `s 552(2) in some other way` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is immaterial how the shares or money are so applied ... or otherwise"

-- src:7656 | (3) Nothing in this section affects the payment of such brokerage as has previously been lawful.
@ref s 552(3) nothing in this section affects the payment of brokerage that has previously been lawful (src:7656)
GIVEN `the payment is of such brokerage as has previously been lawful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 552(3) section 552 affects the payment of the brokerage` MEANS
    IF `the payment is of such brokerage as has previously been lawful`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section affects the payment of such brokerage as has previously been lawful"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such brokerage as has previously been lawful"

§§ `Registration of allotment and return of allotment (ss 554 to 557)`

-- ---- s 558: When shares are allotted (written first: the dates below are its dates) ----------------------

-- src:7713 | For the purposes of the Companies Acts shares in a company are taken to be allotted when a person acquires the unconditional right to be included in the company's register of members ... in respect of the shares.
@ref s 558 shares are taken to be allotted when a person acquires the unconditional right to be included in the register of members (src:7713)
GIVEN `a person has acquired the unconditional right to be included in the company's register of members in respect of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 558 the shares are taken to be allotted` MEANS
    IF `a person has acquired the unconditional right to be included in the company's register of members in respect of the shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shares in a company are taken to be allotted when a person acquires the unconditional right" (a "when" that is not met counts as a "where" that fails)

@ref s 558 the time of allotment is the time the unconditional right is acquired (src:7713)
GIVEN `the date on which a person acquires the unconditional right to be included in the company's register of members in respect of the shares` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 558 the date on which the shares are taken to be allotted` MEANS
    `the date on which a person acquires the unconditional right to be included in the company's register of members in respect of the shares`

-- ---- s 554: Registration of allotment --------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7669 | (2) This does not apply if the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares (see section 779).
@ref s 554(2) the duty to register does not apply if a share warrant has been issued (src:7669)
GIVEN `the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 554(2) the duty in section 554(1) does not apply` MEANS
    IF `the company has issued a share warrant in respect of the shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This does not apply if the company has issued a share warrant" (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))

-- src:7668 | (1) A company must register an allotment of shares as soon as practicable and in any event within two months after the date of the allotment.
@ref s 554(1) a company must register an allotment as soon as practicable and within two months (src:7668)
GIVEN `s 554(2) the duty in section 554(1) does not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the date of the allotment` IS A DATE
      `the company has registered the allotment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the company registered the allotment` IS A DATE
      `the company registered it as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 554(1) the company has complied with the duty to register the allotment` MEANS
    IF `s 554(2) the duty in section 554(1) does not apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the duty does not apply, so there is nothing to fail (fork F-554)
    ELSE IF `the company has registered the allotment`
         THEN IF     `the date on which the company registered the allotment` AT MOST `the last day for registering the allotment`
                 AND `the company registered it as soon as practicable`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "as soon as practicable and in any event within two months after the date of the allotment" (a period fixed in its own words, and a bare "must" not done)
         ELSE IF `the date on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `the last day for registering the allotment`
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in any event within two months after the date of the allotment" (the period has ended and the allotment is not registered)
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the two months have not ended, so the text does not yet say the company has failed
    WHERE
        `the last day for registering the allotment` MEANS `add months` `the date of the allotment` 2

-- src:7671 | (3) If a company fails to comply with this section, an offence is committed by—
-- src:7672 | (a) the company, and
-- src:7673 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 554(3) offence: if a company fails to comply, the company and every officer in default (src:7671-7673)
GIVEN `s 554(1) the company has complied with the duty to register the allotment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 554(3)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 554(1) the company has complied with the duty to register the allotment`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with this section, an offence is committed" (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the company has not yet failed to comply

@ref s 554(3)(b) offence: every officer of the company who is in default (src:7673)
GIVEN `s 554(1) the company has complied with the duty to register the allotment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 554(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 554(1) the company has complied with the duty to register the allotment`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
        CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 1121 is not among the sources
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with this section, an offence is committed" (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the company has not yet failed to comply

-- src:7674 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 554(4) penalty: summary conviction, level 3, and a daily default fine of one-tenth of level 3 (src:7674)
`s 554(4) penalty on summary conviction` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
    `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
    `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
    `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

@ref s 554(4) the most a person can be fined, in pounds, for one conviction and for each day of continued contravention (src:7674)
GIVEN `the amount in pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 554(4) the most the fine can be, in pounds` MEANS `the amount in pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for`

@ref s 554(4) the daily default fine, in pounds (src:7674)
GIVEN `the amount in pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 554(4) the most the daily default fine can be, in pounds` MEANS `the amount in pounds that level 3 on the standard scale stands for` TIMES 0.1

-- ---- s 555: Return of allotment by limited company -------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7678 | (1) This section applies to a company limited by shares and to a company limited by guarantee and having a share capital.
@ref s 555(1) the section applies to a company limited by shares and to a company limited by guarantee with a share capital (src:7678)
GIVEN `the company's profile` IS A `Company profile`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 555(1) section 555 applies to the company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the company's profile`'s `liability of the members`
    WHEN `liability limited to the amount, if any, unpaid on the shares held` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `liability limited to the amount the members undertake to contribute on a winding up` THEN
        IF `the company's profile`'s `a share capital`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): a company limited by guarantee that has no share capital is not named, and the text does not say "only"
    WHEN `liability not limited` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): an unlimited company is not named (section 556 is its section), and the text does not say "only"
    WHEN `liability limited in some other way by the constitution` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): not named

-- src:7679 | (2) The company must, within one month of making an allotment of shares, deliver to the registrar for registration a return of the allotment.
@ref s 555(2) the company must within one month of making an allotment deliver a return of the allotment (src:7679)
GIVEN `s 1072 the document meets the requirements for proper delivery` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1071 the day the registrar received the document` IS A DATE
      `the date of the allotment` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 555(2) the company has delivered the return of the allotment in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1072 the document meets the requirements for proper delivery`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `s 1071 the day the registrar received the document` AT MOST `the last day for delivering the return`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within one month of making an allotment of shares" (a period fixed in its own words; the return was delivered after it)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
        IF `the date on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `the last day for delivering the return`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within one month of making an allotment of shares" (the month has ended and no proper return has been delivered)
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the month has not ended, so the text does not yet say the company has failed
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 1072 is not among the sources
    WHERE
        `the last day for delivering the return` MEANS `add months` `the date of the allotment` 1

-- src:7681 | (a) contain the prescribed information, and
@ref s 555(3)(a) the return must contain the prescribed information (src:7681)
GIVEN `the return contains the prescribed information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 555(3)(a) the return meets the requirement to contain the prescribed information` MEANS
    IF `the return contains the prescribed information`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The return must (a) contain the prescribed information" (a bare "must" not done: a fork line; what is prescribed is outside the sources)

-- src:7682 | (b) be accompanied by a statement of capital.
@ref s 555(3)(b) the return must be accompanied by a statement of capital (src:7682)
GIVEN `the return is accompanied by a statement of capital` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 555(3)(b) the return meets the requirement to be accompanied by a statement of capital` MEANS
    IF `the return is accompanied by a statement of capital`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The return must ... (b) be accompanied by a statement of capital" (a bare "must" not done: a fork line)

-- src:7684 | (a) the total number of shares of the company,
-- src:7685 | (b) the aggregate nominal value of those shares,
-- src:7686 | (ba) the aggregate amount (if any) unpaid on those shares (whether on account of their nominal value or by way of premium), and
-- src:7687 | (c) for each class of shares—
-- src:7688 | (i) prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares,
-- src:7689 | (ii) the total number of shares of that class, and
-- src:7690 | (iii) the aggregate nominal value of shares of that class, ...
@ref s 555(4) the statement of capital must state the company's share capital at the date to which the return is made up (src:7684-7690)
GIVEN `it states the total number of shares of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states the aggregate nominal value of those shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states the aggregate amount (if any) unpaid on those shares (whether on account of their nominal value or by way of premium)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for each class of shares, it states prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for each class of shares, it states the total number of shares of that class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for each class of shares, it states the aggregate nominal value of shares of that class` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 555(4) the statement of capital meets the requirements of subsection (4)` MEANS
    IF     `it states the total number of shares of the company`
       AND `it states the aggregate nominal value of those shares`
       AND `it states the aggregate amount (if any) unpaid on those shares (whether on account of their nominal value or by way of premium)`
       AND `for each class of shares, it states prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares`
       AND `for each class of shares, it states the total number of shares of that class`
       AND `for each class of shares, it states the aggregate nominal value of shares of that class`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statement of capital must state ... (a) ... (b) ... (ba) ... and (c) for each class of shares ..." (a bare "must" not done: a fork line)

-- ---- s 556: Return of allotment by unlimited company allotting new class of shares -----------------------

-- src:7696 | (4) For the purposes of this section shares are not to be treated as different from shares previously allotted by reason only that the former do not carry the same rights to dividends as the latter during the twelve months immediately following the former's allotment.
@ref s 556(4) shares are not treated as different by reason only of a difference in dividend rights in the first twelve months (src:7696)
GIVEN `the only difference is that the new shares do not carry the same rights to dividends as the shares previously allotted during the twelve months immediately following their allotment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 556(4) the difference in rights is disregarded` MEANS
    IF `the only difference is that the new shares do not carry the same rights to dividends as the shares previously allotted during the twelve months immediately following their allotment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only that the former do not carry the same rights to dividends as the latter during the twelve months immediately following the former's allotment"

-- src:7693 | (1) This section applies to an unlimited company that allots shares of a class with rights that are not in all respects uniform with shares previously allotted.
@ref s 556(1) the section applies to an unlimited company that allots shares of a class with rights not in all respects uniform (src:7693)
GIVEN `s 3(4) the company is an unlimited company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are of a class with rights that are not in all respects uniform with shares previously allotted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 556(4) the difference in rights is disregarded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 556(1) section 556 applies to the allotment` MEANS
    IF `s 3(4) the company is an unlimited company` AND `the shares are of a class with rights that are not in all respects uniform with shares previously allotted`
    THEN IF `s 556(4) the difference in rights is disregarded` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shares are not to be treated as different from shares previously allotted by reason only that the former do not carry the same rights to dividends"
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to an unlimited company that allots shares of a class with rights that are not in all respects uniform"

-- src:7694 | (2) The company must, within one month of making such an allotment, deliver to the registrar for registration a return of the allotment.
@ref s 556(2) the company must within one month of making such an allotment deliver a return (src:7694)
GIVEN `s 1072 the document meets the requirements for proper delivery` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1071 the day the registrar received the document` IS A DATE
      `the date of the allotment` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 556(2) the company has delivered the return of the allotment in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1072 the document meets the requirements for proper delivery`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `s 1071 the day the registrar received the document` AT MOST `the last day for delivering the return`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within one month of making such an allotment" (a period fixed in its own words; the return was delivered after it)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
        IF `the date on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `the last day for delivering the return`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within one month of making such an allotment" (the month has ended and no proper return has been delivered)
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the month has not ended, so the text does not yet say the company has failed
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 1072 is not among the sources
    WHERE
        `the last day for delivering the return` MEANS `add months` `the date of the allotment` 1

-- src:7695 | (3) The return must contain the prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares.
@ref s 556(3) the return must contain the prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares (src:7695)
GIVEN `the return contains the prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 556(3) the return meets the requirement to contain the prescribed particulars of the rights` MEANS
    IF `the return contains the prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The return must contain the prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares" (a bare "must" not done: a fork line)

-- ---- s 557: Offence of failure to make return ------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7698 | (1) If a company makes default in complying with—
-- src:7699 | section 555 (return of allotment of shares by limited company), or
-- src:7700 | section 556 (return of allotment of new class of shares by unlimited company),
-- src:7701 | an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 557(1) offence: if a company makes default in complying with s 555 or s 556, every officer in default (src:7698-7701)
GIVEN `s 555(2) the company has delivered the return of the allotment in time` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 556(2) the company has delivered the return of the allotment in time` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 557(1) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `s 555(2) the company has delivered the return of the allotment in time` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `s 556(2) the company has delivered the return of the allotment in time` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 1121 is not among the sources
    ELSE IF `s 555(2) the company has delivered the return of the allotment in time` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 556(2) the company has delivered the return of the allotment in time` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company makes default in complying with section 555 ... or section 556 ..." (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): neither return duty is shown to have been defaulted in

-- src:7702 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:7703 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:7704 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of the statutory maximumone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or the amount corresponding to level 4 on the standard scale for summary offences.
@ref s 557(2) penalty: on indictment a fine; on summary conviction a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum and a daily default fine (src:7702-7704)
`s 557(2)(a) penalty on conviction on indictment` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
    `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
    `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
    `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

-- The text of s 557(2)(b) shows two readings of the daily default fine run together ("one-tenth of the statutory maximum" and
-- "one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or the amount corresponding to level 4 on the standard scale for summary offences"); it does
-- not say which is in force (fork F-557(2)(b)). So the daily fine in the penalty below is NOTHING (the text does not choose), and
-- each reading has a function of its own, in pounds.
@ref s 557(2)(b) penalty on summary conviction (src:7704)
`s 557(2)(b) penalty on summary conviction` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
    `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)
    `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text shows two readings and does not choose between them
    `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

@ref s 557(2)(b) daily default fine, first reading: one-tenth of the statutory maximum (src:7704)
GIVEN `the amount in pounds that the statutory maximum stands for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 557(2)(b) the most the daily default fine can be, in pounds, on the reading one-tenth of the statutory maximum` MEANS
    `the amount in pounds that the statutory maximum stands for` TIMES 0.1

@ref s 557(2)(b) daily default fine, second reading: one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or the amount for level 4 (src:7704)
GIVEN `the amount in pounds that level 4 on the standard scale stands for, for summary offences` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 557(2)(b) the most the daily default fine can be, in pounds, on the reading one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 and level 4` MEANS
    (max 5000 `the amount in pounds that level 4 on the standard scale stands for, for summary offences`) TIMES 0.1

@ref s 557(2) a person guilty of an offence under s 557 is liable (src:7702-7704)
GIVETH A LIST OF Penalty
`s 557(2) the penalties for an offence under section 557` MEANS
    LIST `s 557(2)(a) penalty on conviction on indictment`, `s 557(2)(b) penalty on summary conviction`

-- src:7705 | (3) In the case of default in delivering to the registrar within one month after the allotment the return required by section 555 or 556—
-- src:7706 | (a) any person liable for the default may apply to the court for relief, and
@ref s 557(3)(a) a person liable for the default may apply to the court for relief (src:7705-7706)
GIVEN `the person is liable for the default` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the default is in delivering to the registrar within one month after the allotment the return required by section 555 or 556` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 557(3)(a) the person may apply to the court for relief` MEANS
    IF `the person is liable for the default` AND `the default is in delivering to the registrar within one month after the allotment the return required by section 555 or 556`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person liable for the default may apply to the court for relief" in the case of default in delivering the return within one month

-- src:7707 | (b) the court, if satisfied—
-- src:7708 | (i) that the omission to deliver the document was accidental or due to inadvertence, or
-- src:7709 | (ii) that it is just and equitable to grant relief,
-- src:7710 | may make an order extending the time for delivery of the document for such period as the court thinks proper.
@ref s 557(3)(b) the court, if satisfied, may extend the time for delivery (src:7707-7710)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the omission to deliver the document was accidental or due to inadvertence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that it is just and equitable to grant relief` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 557(3)(b) the court may make an order extending the time for delivery` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied that the omission to deliver the document was accidental or due to inadvertence` OR `the court is satisfied that it is just and equitable to grant relief`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court, if satisfied (i) ... or (ii) ..., may make an order" (a grant: a failed condition is not the text's no, fork F-grant-gate)

-- ---- s 559: Provisions about allotment not applicable to shares taken on formation -----------------------

-- src:7715 | The provisions of this Chapter have no application in relation to the taking of shares by the subscribers to the memorandum on the formation of the company.
@ref s 559 the provisions of this Chapter have no application to the shares taken by the subscribers on formation (src:7715)
GIVEN `the shares are taken by the subscribers to the memorandum on the formation of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 559 the provisions of Chapter 2 apply to the taking of the shares` MEANS
    IF `the shares are taken by the subscribers to the memorandum on the formation of the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The provisions of this Chapter have no application in relation to the taking of shares by the subscribers to the memorandum on the formation of the company"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section speaks of the taking of shares by the subscribers only
